=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play ssh/root-session ----------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: ssh/root-session$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13 (OpenSSH 10.0p2). debian13,$
# but hardn runs from root's own SSH login, by key: no$
# SUDO_USER.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [ ] SSH Login            Partial root key-only$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [ ] SSH Port             Not Configured default (22)$
$
  SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Key only sshd's default$
   -  Password Login       Off by sshd_config$
   -  SSH Port             22$
   -  Allowed Users        Anyone$
   -  Logged in as         root, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disallow root login  Root can't log in over SSH$
   2) Password login on    Let passwords log in again$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# You're logged in as root over SSH. Turning root login off$
# would close the way you came in. Log in as an admin and run$
# hardn through sudo.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [ ] SSH Login            Partial root key-only$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [ ] SSH Port             Not Configured default (22)$
$
  SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Key only sshd's default$
   -  Password Login       Off by sshd_config$
   -  SSH Port             22$
   -  Allowed Users        Anyone$
   -  Logged in as         root, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disallow root login  Root can't log in over SSH$
   2) Password login on    Let passwords log in again$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

